      "text": "San Salvador, Cerro Verde and the Route of Flowers"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:569e72e117968fcc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "57a73568abb5ade483ef414e1b6f1a63851134d825975c7710dff53d2f7a9ef3",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw96knej-0c36k4xy7k",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, you’ll explore San Salvador’s historic centre. You’ll see El Rosario Church, the National Palace, the National Theatre and the Metropolitan Cathedral, where Archbishop Óscar Romero is buried.\n\nYou’ll then visit El Boquerón National Park at the crater of the San Salvador volcano and continue to Los Volcanes National Park. Here you’ll find cloud forests, wild orchids and panoramic views of Lake Coatepeque and the Izalco volcano.\n\nIn the afternoon, you’ll drive into the mountains along the Ruta de las Flores, or Route of Flowers, through a region of coffee plantations, forests and villages in bloom.\n\nOvernight at Hotel Fleur de Lis. Meals: breakfast."
    },
